---
/**
 * What used to be a full section of transport/identity/runtime controls plus a
 * twelve-abbreviation tag cloud. None of it was wrong; all of it was reference
 * material read by someone already convinced, which is not what a landing page
 * is for. It lives at /security now, in full and with the honest gaps.
 */
---

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pb-32">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-900/20 px-7 py-6 text-center">
    <p class="text-zinc-400">
      TLS and custom CAs, SSRF refused at connect time, JWKS-validated identity, rate
      limiting, value-level secret redaction — and the standards behind them, mapped
      against the OWASP MCP Top 10 including the three categories Hangar deliberately
      does not cover.
    </p>
    <a
      href="/security"
      class="group inline-flex items-center gap-2 mt-4 text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-300 hover:text-zinc-100 transition-colors"
    >
      Security, in full
      <span class="transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
